{
  "id": "LUK.13",
  "number": "13",
  "bookId": "LUK",
  "reference": "Luke 13",
  "verseCount": 35,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "13",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "LUK 13"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "13",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Now there were some present at that very season who told him of the Galilæans, whose blood Pilate had mingled with their sacrifices. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he answered and said unto them, Think ye that these Galilæans were sinners above all the Galilæans, because they have suffered these things? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I tell you, Nay: but, except ye repent, ye shall all in like manner perish. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Or those eighteen, upon whom the tower in Siloam fell, and killed them, think ye that they were offenders above all the men that dwell in Jerusalem? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I tell you, Nay: but, except ye repent, ye shall all likewise perish.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.5"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he spake this parable; A certain man had a fig tree planted in his vineyard; and he came seeking fruit thereon, and found none. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he said unto the vinedresser, Behold, these three years I come seeking fruit on this fig tree, and find none: cut it down; why doth it also cumber the ground? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he answering saith unto him, Lord, let it alone this year also, till I shall dig about it, and dung it: ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and if it bear fruit thenceforth, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "; but if not, thou shalt cut it down.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.9"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he was teaching in one of the synagogues on the sabbath day. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And behold, a woman that had a spirit of infirmity eighteen years; and she was bowed together, and could in no wise lift herself up. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And when Jesus saw her, he called her, and said to her, Woman, thou art loosed from thine infirmity. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he laid his hands upon her: and immediately she was made straight, and glorified God. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And the ruler of the synagogue, being moved with indignation because Jesus had healed on the sabbath, answered and said to the multitude, There are six days in which men ought to work: in them therefore come and be healed, and not on the day of the sabbath. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But the Lord answered him, and said, Ye hypocrites, doth not each one of you on the sabbath loose his ox or his ass from the stall, and lead him away to watering? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And ought not this woman, being a daughter of Abraham, whom Satan had bound, lo, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " eighteen years, to have been loosed from this bond on the day of the sabbath? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And as he said these things, all his adversaries were put to shame: and all the multitude rejoiced for all the glorious things that were done by him.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.17"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He said therefore, Unto what is the kingdom of God like? and whereunto shall I liken it? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "It is like unto a grain of mustard seed, which a man took, and cast into his own garden; and it grew, and became a tree; and the birds of the heaven lodged in the branches thereof.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.19"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And again he said, Whereunto shall I liken the kingdom of God? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "It is like unto leaven, which a woman took and hid in three measures of meal, till it was all leavened.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.21"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he went on his way through cities and villages, teaching, and journeying on unto Jerusalem. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And one said unto him, Lord, are they few that are saved? And he said unto them, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "24",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:24"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "24",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Strive to enter in by the narrow door: for many, I say unto you, shall seek to enter in, and shall not be able. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.24"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "25",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:25"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "25",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "When once the master of the house is risen up, and hath shut to the door, and ye begin to stand without, and to knock at the door, saying, Lord, open to us; and he shall answer and say to you, I know you not whence ye are; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.25"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "26",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:26"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "26",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "then shall ye begin to say, We did eat and drink in thy presence, and thou didst teach in our streets; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.26"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "27",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:27"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "27",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and he shall say, I tell you, I know not whence ye are; depart from me, all ye workers of iniquity. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.27",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.27"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "28",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:28"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "28",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "There shall be the weeping and the gnashing of teeth, when ye shall see Abraham, and Isaac, and Jacob, and all the prophets, in the kingdom of God, and yourselves cast forth without. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.28",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.28"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "29",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:29"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "29",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And they shall come from the east and west, and from the north and south, and shall sit down in the kingdom of God. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.29",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.29"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "30",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:30"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "30",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And behold, there are last who shall be first, and there are first who shall be last.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.30",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.30"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "30",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:30"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "30",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.30",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.30"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "31",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:31"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "31",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In that very hour there came certain Pharisees, saying to him, Get thee out, and go hence: for Herod would fain kill thee. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.31",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.31"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "32",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:32"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "32",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he said unto them, Go and say to that fox, Behold, I cast out demons and perform cures to-day and to-morrow, and the third ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.32",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.32"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " I am perfected. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.32",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.32"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "33",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:33"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "33",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Nevertheless I must go on my way to-day and to-morrow and the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.33",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.33"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " following: for it cannot be that a prophet perish out of Jerusalem. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.33",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.33"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "34",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:34"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "34",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "O Jerusalem, Jerusalem, that killeth the prophets, and stoneth them that are sent unto her! how often would I have gathered thy children together, even as a hen ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.34",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.34"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " her own brood under her wings, and ye would not! ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.34",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.34"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "35",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 13:35"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "35",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Behold, your house is left unto you ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.35",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.35"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ": and I say unto you, Ye shall not see me, until ye shall say, Blessed ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.35",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.35"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " he that cometh in the name of the Lord.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.13.35",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.13.35"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
